Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with specialized partners, proposes a comprehensive artificial intelligence (AI) solution to assist the City of Belval's municipal agents. Our proposal integrates AI capabilities, data sovereignty, security, and sustainability, aligning with the city's digital transformation strategy and regulatory requirements.

# Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval requires an intelligent assistance tool for its agents, enhancing access to information, improving answer quality, and reducing processing times. The solution must comply with GDPR, ensure data sovereignty, and integrate with existing systems. The project budget is €3 million over 4 years, with a focus on minimizing environmental footprint.

# Proposed Solution
Our AI-powered solution leverages Large Language Models (LLMs), specifically Mistral 7B Instruct, which can be self-hosted within the European Union to ensure data sovereignty and compliance with GDPR. This model will facilitate access to information, improve answer quality, and reduce processing times for municipal agents. The solution integrates with existing business software, electronic document management systems, and user directories through API interfaces.

For security and compliance, we adhere to ISO 27001 certification standards, ensuring the protection of sensitive data through encryption or anonymization. Our data residency policy aligns with the City of Belval's requirement for hosting data exclusively within the EU. We also conduct Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs) to identify and mitigate any data protection risks.

The technical architecture is designed to provide high availability (99.9%) and fast response times (less than 2 seconds), utilizing Docker, Kubernetes (K8s), Helm, Prometheus, Grafana, and the ELK Stack for monitoring and logging. We ensure compliance with security requirements through our experience with SecNumCloud infrastructure or equivalent.

Our budget is €3 million over 4 years, with a projected gross margin percentage of 28%. We deliver high-quality services while optimizing costs and achieving a satisfactory margin within the constraints provided. The annual cost of exploitation will be mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority.

For AI innovation, we propose a proactive regulatory change alerting system, enhancing our AI-powered solution that leverages Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) capabilities to provide intelligent assistance to agents. Our approach prioritizes explicability and transparency, ensuring insights into the decision-making process.

Regarding sustainability, we focus on reducing environmental footprint by using low-carbon impact infrastructures. Our hosting solutions are powered by 100% renewable energy. We implement digital sobriety practices such as int8/int4 model quantization, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle.

# Unaddressed Requirements
There are no explicitly unaddressed requirements from the tender, as our proposal covers all aspects of the City of Belval's needs, including AI capabilities, data sovereignty, security, sustainability, and budgetary constraints.

# Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with its partners, offers a comprehensive and innovative AI solution that meets the City of Belval's requirements for intelligent assistance, data sovereignty, security, and sustainability. Our proposal ensures compliance with regulatory frameworks, minimizes environmental footprint, and optimizes costs while delivering high-quality services. We are confident that our solution will enhance the efficiency of the city's administrative services and improve the quality of service rendered to users.
